    <li><a name="2" id="2"></a>Bayer, Amanda, and Cecilia Elena Rouse, &ldquo;Diversity in the Economics Profession: A New Attack on an Old Problem,&rdquo;<em> Journal of Economic Perspectives</em>, Vol. 30, No. 4, Fall 2016, <a href="https://www.aeaweb.org/articles?id=10.1257/jep.30.4.221">https://www.aeaweb.org/articles?id=10.1257/jep.30.4.221</a>.</li>
    <li><a name="3" id="3"></a>Federal Reserve Bank of New York, &ldquo;Who Is Being Trained in Economics? The Race, Ethnicity, and Gender of Economics Majors at U.S. Colleges and Universities,&rdquo; <a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/data-and-statistics/data-visualization/diversity-in-economics#interactive/overview">https://www.newyorkfed.org/data-and-statistics/data-visualization/diversity-in-economics#interactive/overview</a>.</li>
